{
 "_doc": [
  "Named RAM variables and structures used by all three modules. tools/romdis.py resolves every memory operand",
  "to one of these: it tracks DS/ES per instruction (segment loads inside the function, incoming values agreed by",
  "all callers, constant segment words read from ROM), converts seg:off to a linear address and looks it up in",
  "the regions below. Structures are applied to base-register operands ([bp+n], [bx+n]) inside the listed code.",
  "Names print in the listing comment column as region.name (a trailing ? means the segment was assumed, not",
  "proven) and become equ symbols in the NASM sources.",
  "regions: linear start/end (hex), optional 'auto' naming for unnamed offsets ('ivt' = int NNh vector off/seg),",
  "vars keyed by offset relative to the region start: name, optional size (bytes) and comment."
 ],
